          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A witness observed on September 26, 2009 at 11:11 a very bright, silver ball moving very slowly horizontally in the sky. It disappeared instantly. This observation is likely that of a sunlit balloon. With no wind, it could be a relatively close child's balloon or fairground balloon that suddenly burst, or a distant weather balloon high in the sky. This case is classified B as a probable observation of a sunlit balloon.",
